hem **contradictory**: the bitwarden pair disagrees on whether the `bw` CLI is deprecated, and `delegation-research`/`research-delegation` have byte-identical descriptions but different routing tables (Milena/Nadia with pinned models vs a task-type split across Mikhail/Declan/Viktor) — which one an agent loads is a coin flip. |\n\n## 2. Prioritized plan (effort × impact)\n\n1. **Add a `validate-skills` linter + CI** (M effort, very high impact) — error tier: YAML parses, name==folder, required fields, ≥3 tags, related_skills resolve; warning tier: body sections, reciprocity, hardcoded paths. Pre-commit hook + GitHub Action. This is the only item that makes the others permanent.\n2. **Fix the 4 broken YAML frontmatters + 5 name mismatches** (XS, high) — one-line quoting fixes restore discovery for 4 skills.\n3. **Merge the 5 duplicate pairs, contradictory ones first** (S–M, high) — keep the richer skill, leave a tombstone SKILL.md with `superseded_by:` so crons and links don't break.\n4. **Script-fix the 39 dangling refs** (S, medium-high) — stripping the `vladislava-` prefix is mechanical; ~10 others (`codex`, `financial-report`, …) need hand resolution.\n5. **Pick one tag schema and migrate** (S, high) — recommend flipping AGENTS.md to top-level `tags:` (the 34-skill majority, simpler shape) and script-migrating the 20 hermes-schema skills.\n6. **Backfill the 10 stubs** (M, medium) — start with `playwright-cli` and `brainrepo`, each sitting on 9 orphaned reference/script files their bodies never index.\n7. **Path-portability sweep** (L, medium) — per the AGENTS.md Part 5 patch table; do the most-used skills first and let the linter's warning tier ratchet the rest rather than big-bang rewriting 45 skills.\n\n## 3. Governance to prevent recurrence\n\nCI-as-spec (rules not in the linter get ignored); a `TEMPLATE/SKILL.md` + scaffold script (stubs happen because authoring starts from blank); a rename policy requiring repo-wide `related_skills` grep (the entire dangling-ref problem traces to one missed step); a tombstone deprecation policy; a stub policy (backfill within two weeks or move out of the discovery root); and updating AGENTS.md to match whichever tag schema wins.\n\n## 4. Patch-first shortlist\n\n(1) `bitwarden`+`bitwarden-secrets` — contradictory secret-handling guidance is the riskiest single defect; (2) `delegation-research`+`research-delegation`; (3) the four one-line YAML fixes; (4) tombstone `forge-github-model-sync` (script-less copy); (5) `research-local-gemma`/`local-gemma-sidecar`; (6) `doccontrol`/`kovaforge-doccontrol`; (7) bodies for `playwright-cli` and `brainrepo`.\n\n## 5. Verification & self-score\n\nExecuting items 1–5 is roughly two short sessions and is directly measurable: rerun the audit parser and criteria 1, 2, 3, and 7 should each reach 8+, moving the repo from ≈4.3 to ≈7. The baseline numbers for that comparison are stored in both the repo report and my memory file.\n\n**Plan self-score: 8.5/10.** Strengths: every claim is backed by a verified count or a confirmed diff, the top fixes are mechanical/scriptable, and the lift is measurable against a recorded baseline. Held back from higher: I reviewed rather than executed (even the four one-line YAML fixes remain to be applied), and the CI recommendation assumes GitHub Actions is available on the private `KovaForge/skills` remote, which I did not verify.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"74abbb81-55ae-4497-8885-6c6086be9eda","total_cost_usd":1.825157,"usage":{"input_tokens":2102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34876,"cache_read_input_tokens":329709,"output_tokens":15517,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34876,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2216,"cache_read_input_tokens":42255,"cache_creation_input_tokens":772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephe